# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  GUEST PHOTO UPLOADS (Cloudinary)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in both values.
#  Full walkthrough: README-PHOTOS.md
#
#  Leave either blank and the photo section hides itself — the
#  rest of the invitation is unaffected.
#
#  Both values are PUBLIC by design. They are inlined into the
#  browser bundle, because that is where the upload happens.
#  Neither is a credential: the preset grants permission to add
#  files under rules you set, and nothing else. Never put your
#  Cloudinary API SECRET in this file — it is not needed here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Cloudinary cloud name — Dashboard → Product Environment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=

# The UNSIGNED upload preset you created. See README-PHOTOS.md step 2.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=
